rmal**\n- **CRP not elevated**\n\n**Renal ultrasound**\n- **Mild right hydronephrosis**\n- **Possible small proximal ureteral stone**, not directly visualized\n- **No renal mass seen**\n\n## Interpretation\nThis synthetic pattern is **most compatible with a small right-sided ureteral stone causing partial urinary obstruction**. That impression is supported by the flank discomfort, trace blood in the urine, prior stone history, and mild hydronephrosis on ultrasound.\n\nThat said, this remains **preliminary rather than definitive**:\n- the stone was **suspected but not directly seen**\n- the current data do **not strongly support infection**\n- kidney function appears **preserved**\n- the lack of a renal mass on ultrasound is **reassuring** in this synthetic case\n\n## Red Flags\nMore urgent medical review would be appropriate if any of these develop:\n- **fever or chills**\n- **vomiting** or inability to keep fluids down\n- **worsening or severe pain**\n- **reduced urine output**\n- **visible blood in the urine**\n- feeling suddenly much more unwell\n\n## Suggested Next Steps\n- Arrange **clinical follow-up soon**\n- Maintain **good hydration**\n- Monitor symptoms for worsening or red flags\n- If symptoms persist or remain unclear, a clinician may consider **additional evaluation or imaging**\n\n**Bottom line:** in this synthetic test case, the distilled output leans toward a **small right ureteral stone with mild obstruction**, without current evidence of kidney failure, infection, or a renal mass. This is still a **preliminary indicator**, not a final diagnosis.\n\nIf you want, I can now:\n1. turn this into a **shorter patient-facing report**, or  \n2. help you format the **exact synthetic context + diagnostic input payload** for future Doctor Agent runs.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_021fa6657b4239000169c41a2f6b3081919f997b751ffed1b4\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"inpu