since:\\n\\n• no fever was reported\\n• inflammatory markers were not elevated\\n• urine infection markers were negative\\n\\nKidney function appears preserved, which is reassuring, and the ultrasound did not show a renal mass.\\n\\nRed Flags\\n\\nUrgent in-person care would be appropriate if any of these occur:\\n\\n• fever or chills\\n• worsening or severe pain\\n• persistent vomiting\\n• difficulty urinating or marked drop in urine output\\n• visible heavy blood in urine\\n• fainting, worsening weakness, or signs of dehydration\\n\\nSuggested Next Steps\\n\\n• Arrange clinical follow-up soon\\n• A clinician may consider repeat assessment and decide whether more imaging is needed if symptoms continue or worsen\\n• Hydration status may be worth reviewing, unless fluid restriction has already been advised\\n\\nTool-used status: no — the Doctor Agent reported that it attempted to run the real llm_distillator workflow, but it was not usable in this environment because the underlying access token had expired.\\n\\nIf you want, I can now help you:\\n\\n1. draft a fix request for the expired token issue, or\\n2. prepare a clean synthetic payload so you can retry the real llm_distillator tool once access is restored.\"\n}\n```\n\nwhy it was not able to run the distillation tool?"}],"timestamp":1774459594407}}
